cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark, its measurements or its code, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "flyvis-circuit-bench: a benchmark of circuit-discovery methods against ablation ground truth in the flyvis connectome model"
abstract: >-
  In the flyvis model of the fly visual system, each of the 604 cell-type-to-cell-type connection classes is
  ablated and the change of the network response is the ground truth. Across 10 trained models, ranking
  connections by synapse count recovers 53% of the achievable signal, the sum of trained weights 76%, a single
  gradient 92% and attribution patching 97%. The decision rules were written before the data; negative results,
  including a refuted mechanism hypothesis, are reported. The repository includes a leaderboard and a tool to
  score new methods.
authors:
